[2026-03-14T21:39:11.699Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PqfKTypcunnc3joXwHsKMJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Setting Up Replay with Playwright\n\n## Installation Steps\n\nBegin by installing the Replay Playwright plugin using your preferred package manager:\n\n```sh\nnpm install --save-dev @replayio/playwright\n```\n\nThen install the Replay Browser itself:\n\n```sh\nnpx replayio install\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nCreate a Test Suite Team at https://app.replay.io/team/new/tests to obtain an API key. Store it in a `.env` file as `REPLAY_API_KEY=<your_api_key>` (recommended approach).\n\n## Configuration\n\nUpdate your `playwright.config.ts` file to incorporate the Replay reporter and browser. The key imports needed are:\n\n```typescript\nimport { replayReporter, devices as replayDevices } from \"@replayio/playwright\";\n```\n\nAdd these to your PlaywrightTestConfig:\n\n- **Reporter**: Include `replayReporter({ apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY, upload: true })`\n- **Project**: Add a `replay-chromium` project using `replayDevices[\"Replay Chromium\"]`\n\nThe setting `\"upload: true\"` ensures recordings are automatically transmitted after test completion. Preserve existing projects and reporters alongside these new Replay components.\n\n## Running Tests\n\nExecute tests with the Replay Browser using:\n\n```sh\nnpx playwright test --project replay-chromium\n```\n\nThe configured reporter automatically uploads recordings once testing concludes, making them available for debugging and performance analysis in the Replay interface."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9de3f4b-08be-4be3-914c-363c5ef7580e","uuid":"b48e6dbb-4f7f-43c0-92af-4d22cc53c9e0","tool_use_result":{"bytes":5167,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Setting Up Replay with Playwright\n\n## Installation Steps\n\nBegin by installing the Replay Playwright plugin using your preferred package manager:\n\n```sh\nnpm install --save-dev @replayio/playwright\n```\n\nThen install the Replay Browser itself:\n\n```sh\nnpx replayio install\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nCreate a Test Suite Team at https://app.replay.io/team/new/tests to obtain an API key. Store it in a `.env` file as `REPLAY_API_KEY=<your_api_key>` (recommended approach).\n\n## Configuration\n\nUpdate your `playwright.config.ts` file to incorporate the Replay reporter and browser. The key imports needed are:\n\n```typescript\nimport { replayReporter, devices as replayDevices } from \"@replayio/playwright\";\n```\n\nAdd these to your PlaywrightTestConfig:\n\n- **Reporter**: Include `replayReporter({ apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY, upload: true })`\n- **Project**: Add a `replay-chromium` project using `replayDevices[\"Replay Chromium\"]`\n\nThe setting `\"upload: true\"` ensures recordings are automatically transmitted after test completion. Preserve existing projects and reporters alongside these new Replay components.\n\n## Running Tests\n\nExecute tests with the Replay Browser using:\n\n```sh\nnpx playwright test --project replay-chromium\n```\n\nThe configured reporter automatically uploads recordings once testing concludes, making them available for debugging and performance analysis in the Replay interface.","durationMs":3707,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-playwright/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T21:39:12.337Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KUx3TGx9kEeqVdigiyTJYe","type":"tool_result","content":"# Instructions for Using Replay MCP Tools\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by following a structured methodology:\n\n## Core Approach\n\nThe recommended process involves four steps:\n1. \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\"\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and support a hypothesis with gathered data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection (find files, read contents, search patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (\"Show the stack frames at a point\" and control dependencies)\n- State details (point descriptions, DOM inspection, React component trees)\n- Expression analysis through logpoints and evaluation\n\n## Key Techniques\n\nWhen investigating code behavior, locate relevant source files, verify execution occurred, and examine execution details. The Logpoint tool proves particularly valuable for \"see[ing] the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed\" to identify unexpected patterns.\n\nFor timing issues, find the associated event point and use ControlDependency to trace prerequisite events and delays."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9de3f4b-08be-4be3-914c-363c5ef7580e","uuid":"7920deda-3148-4b58-83f3-76c6e3145001","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Instructions for Using Replay MCP Tools\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by following a structured methodology:\n\n## Core Approach\n\nThe recommended process involves four steps:\n1. \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\"\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and support a hypothesis with gathered data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection (find files, read contents, search patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (\"Show the stack frames at a point\" and control dependencies)\n- State details (point descriptions, DOM inspection, React component trees)\n- Expression analysis through logpoints and evaluation\n\n## Key Techniques\n\nWhen investigating code behavior, locate relevant source files, verify execution occurred, and examine execution details. The Logpoint tool proves particularly valuable for \"see[ing] the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed\" to identify unexpected patterns.\n\nFor timing issues, find the associated event point and use ControlDependency to trace prerequisite events and delays.","durationMs":3157,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
